     "text": "Each core streams its half of `x` as one 128-partition tile. The doubling alternates between VectorE and ScalarE. I have not compiled or run this file.\n\n- **Split across cores:** under LNC=2 each of the two programs takes one contiguous half of `x`. That half is viewed as a `(128, M)` slab, with `M = n / 256`.\n- **Tiling:** the slab is cut into `(128, F)` column tiles. Each tile is loaded by DMA, doubled in place on chip, and stored straight back to the output.\n  - `F` is `M // 8`, clamped to the range [1024, 4096]. This gives at least 4 tiles per core for pipelining.\n  - Tiles are 256 KiB to 1 MiB per DMA, with rows of at least 2 KiB that are contiguous in HBM.\n  - Peak SBUF use is at most 160 KiB per partition.\n- **Compute engines:** even tiles are doubled on VectorE (`tensor_scalar`, multiply by 2.0). Odd tiles are doubled on ScalarE (`activation` copy with `scale=2.0`). Both are exact for fp16, and splitting keeps compute below the DMA time.\n- **Single pass:** each element is read once and written once, with nothing written to HBM in between.\n- **Edge handling:** a narrower last column tile is handled if one ever occurs. Every configured `n` (a multiple of 2^20) divides evenly, so it should not.\n\n```python\ntitle=\"impl_nki.py\"\nimport torch\nimport nki\nimport nki.language as nl\nimport nki.isa as nisa\n\nP = 128\nN_PROG_EXPECTED = 2  # bare kernel call runs with LNC=2 on this host\n\n_LAST_CONFIG = {}\n\n\ndef _pick_tile(m):\n    # Free-axis tile length (elements per partition per tile).\n    # Aim for >= ~8 tiles per program for pipelining, while keeping each\n    # DMA between 256 KiB and 1 MiB (fp16, 128 partitions).\n    f = m // 8\n    if f < 1024:\n        f = 1024\n    if f > 4096:\n        f = 4096\n    if f > m:\n        f = m\n    if f % 2 == 1 and f > 1:\n        f = f - 1\n    return f\n\n\n@nki.jit\ndef mul2_kernel(x, F):\n    n = x.shape[0]\n    out = nl.ndarray((n,), dtype=x.dtype, buffer=nl.shared_hbm)\n    n_prog = nl.num_programs()\n    pid = nl.program_id(0)\n\n    # Each program owns a contiguous chunk of n / n_prog elements, viewed as\n    # (128, M): partition p holds a contiguous run of M elements.\n    M = n // (n_prog * P)\n    x2 = x.reshape((n_prog * P, M))\n    o2 = out.reshape((n_prog * P, M))\n    r0 = pid * P\n\n    T = (M + F - 1) // F\n    for j in range(T):\n        c0 = j * F\n        w = min(F, M - c0)\n        t = nl.ndarray((P, F), dtype=x.dtype, buffer=nl.sbuf)\n        nisa.dma_copy(dst=t[:, 0:w], src=x2[r0:r0 + P, c0:c0 + w])\n        if j % 2 == 0:\n            nisa.tensor_scalar(dst=t[:, 0:w], data=t[:, 0:w],\n                               op0=nl.multiply, operand0=2.0,\n                               engine=nisa.engine.vector)\n        else:\n            nisa.activation(dst=t[:, 0:w], op=nl.copy, data=t[:, 0:w],\n                            scale=2.0)\n        nisa.dma_copy(dst=o2[r0:r0 + P, c0:c0 + w], src=t[:, 0:w])\n    return out\n\n\ndef run(x: torch.Tensor) -> torch.Tensor:\n    global _LAST_CONFIG\n    n = x.numel()\n    M = n // (N_PROG_EXPECTED * P)\n    F = _pick_tile(M)\n    out = mul2_kernel(x, F)\n    T = (M + F - 1) // F\n    _LAST_CONFIG = {\n        \"programs\": N_PROG_EXPECTED,\n        \"partitions\": P,\n        \"elems_per_partition_per_program\": M,\n        \"tile_free\": F,\n        \"tiles_per_program\": T,\n        \"engines\": \"vector/scalar alternating\",\n    }\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_LAST_CONFIG)\n```",
